 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif near «الرسول» (88:2). 89 is Paradise: light mood and motif only, no garden or river. 90:1-6: the tafsirs differ on «المعذرون» (As-Sa'di gives two readings), so only Al-Muyassar's neutral identification is shown. Al-Muyassar's «النصر والغنيمة» and «بالقتل» are not used. STAGING v4: c1 (87): inside a home by day (Al-Muyassar: they stayed in the houses); three men (the hypocrites) sit down on 87:3 (staying behind), a house plate on 87:4-6 (those who stay behind); the women, children and excused of the gloss are not drawn; nothing is drawn for the sealing of hearts (camera only). c2 (88-89) is kept ambient: 88 names the Messenger with the believers who strove with him (fighting) and 89 is Paradise. c3 (90): a desert camp by day (the Bedouins, «الأعراب»; Al-Muyassar: tribes around Medina). Two groups of three men. The ones who came with excuses stand up on 90:1 under a footsteps plate (they set out; the tafsirs differ on whether their excuse was real, so nothing more is shown); nobody speaks and nobody walks toward an empty side (the excuse was presented to the Messenger, who is never shown or implied). The other group stays sitting (90:7, those who lied and sat); the shot is wide while the Name and the Messenger are recited (90:9-11) and holds on the sitters during the threat (90:12-17); no punishment is drawn. Cover: the Bedouins who came with excuses (90:3)."
 },
